{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"74949af2c237e0661f29c0207e9255003fed6d859800f5c041dadc4d500482cc","digest":{"component_or_area":"store write lock (mkdir + fcntl dual-leg)","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/lock.py","src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py","_mkdir_lock_is_stale","_process_start_time","_pid_alive","_MKDIR_LOCK_STALE_CEILING_S","_mkdir_lock_age_exceeds_ceiling","_reclaim_mkdir_lock","_owner_stamp","_parse_v2_stamp","_acquire_mkdir","fcntl.flock","/proc/<pid>/stat"],"problem_keywords":["stale lock","pid recycling","process start time","mkdir lock","no /proc filesystem","unbounded wedge","lock staleness detection"],"propositions":["On platforms without /proc (macOS), _process_start_time always returns None, making the recycled-pid discriminant unsatisfiable and causing dead holders with recycled pids to be judged fresh indefinitely (unbounded wedge).","When current_start is None and a live pid is detected, the lock verdict is unqualified by start-time correlation and must fall back to the 1h ceiling backstop rather than assume liveness.","A genuinely live owner cannot reach the ceiling check because it still holds the exclusive fcntl leg; reaching the check is evidence of an orphaned lock, so the ceiling cannot break a real live owner.","The lock.py module (798 LOC) exceeded the 800-line cap and required a split: owner-identity/stamp/staleness/reclaim logic moved to lock_owner.py, with one-way dependency from lock.py."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787317482818834001,"uuid":"bfa897d4-9a81-4725-a607-14bb0d3ead94"}